            "rationale": "The new write-off, payment-allocation and small-change rules are in Tier 2 (Accounts.standings, Payments.writeOffSmallChange, Policy.writeOffBelow). But the change also extends the borrowing-block rule inside the Tier 4 CLI. That rule recomputes the member's balance from raw fines, payments and write-offs and compares it to a 5.00 literal. Loans.borrow has no block check in this change set, so Tier 4 is the only place that decides this rule. It also duplicates Accounts.owed and Accounts.isBlocked, and the two computations could disagree. Tier 3 Views.fineStatus also derives a fine's paid/unpaid status from raw amounts.",
